---
import AnswerPage from "../components/AnswerPage.astro";
import { facts } from "../data/site";
import { pageMeta, reviewedLabel } from "../data/seo";
---

<AnswerPage title="Downright press and product facts" trail="Press and facts" updated={reviewedLabel} description={pageMeta.press.description} markdownPath={pageMeta.press.markdownPath ?? "/press.md"}>
  <p>Downright Markdown is a free, open-source native Markdown editor and viewer for macOS. It is designed for files people and coding agents change together.</p>

  <h2>50-word description</h2>
  <p>Downright is a free, MIT-licensed native Markdown reader and editor for macOS. Open ordinary files, preview them from Finder with Quick Look, and review external rewrites with word-level changes. It uses AppKit and TextKit 2, keeps the source file in charge, and requires no account, vault, or cloud sync.</p>

  <h2>150-word description</h2>
  <p>Downright Markdown is a native macOS document surface for the Markdown files people and coding agents change together. It opens ordinary project files directly, renders the source without normalizing it into a database, and moves between reading, editing, and Source Focus on the same text surface. Finder and Quick Look make a README or plan easy to inspect; the <code>down</code> command makes it easy to hand a generated document back to a human. When Claude Code, Codex, a script, or another process rewrites an open file, Downright treats that as a review event: it preserves the local buffer, shows what changed, and asks whether to keep the local version or take the version on disk. Downright is free, MIT licensed, works on macOS {facts.minimumMacOS}+, and does not require an account or network connection for ordinary reading, editing, searching, diffing, and export.</p>

  <h2>Product facts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Platform:</strong> macOS {facts.minimumMacOS} and newer.</li>
    <li><strong>License:</strong> {facts.license}.</li>
    <li><strong>Source:</strong> <a href={facts.repository ?? "/"}>open source on GitHub</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Architecture:</strong> native AppKit and TextKit 2; no WebView.</li>
    <li><strong>Integrations:</strong> Finder, Quick Look, Spotlight, Services, App Intents, and the <code>down</code> CLI.</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> no account or telemetry required; files remain local during ordinary use.</li>
    <li><strong>Formats:</strong> {facts.supportedExtensions.map((extension) => `.${extension}`).join(", ")}.</li>
    <li><strong>Current release:</strong> {facts.version} · <a href="/releases/1.0.16/">release evidence</a>.</li>
  </ul>

